# Build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: without it the context was 651 MB and rising, because the
# stack's persistent data lives inside this directory. Worse, the live gateway
# sockets under hermes-home/profiles/*/ made the daemon emit
#   "Can't add file .../gateway.sock to tar: archive/tar: sockets not supported"
# on every single build.
#
# SAFE BECAUSE: the only things any Dockerfile here COPYs are start-mcu.bash
# (Dockerfile:144) and ide/ (Dockerfile.ide). Everything below is runtime data
# or host state that must never be baked into an image.

# Persistent stack data — bind-mounted at runtime, never copied in.
hermes-home/
workspace/
wiki/
acp-ipc/
souls/

# Secrets must never enter a build context.
.env
*.env

# Local noise.
.git/
*.log
*.md
